---
import sampling from "../../public/data/sampling-benchmarks.json";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const raw = `${base}/data/sampling`;
const speed = (value: number) => `${value.toFixed(2)}×`;
const seconds = (value: number) => `${value.toFixed(value < 1 ? 3 : 2)} s`;
const delta = (metric: string, value: number) => {
  const scaled = metric === "accuracy" ? value * 100 : value;
  const digits = metric === "accuracy" ? 2 : 3;
  const rounded = Number(scaled.toFixed(digits));
  return `${rounded > 0 ? "+" : rounded < 0 ? "−" : ""}${Math.abs(rounded).toFixed(digits)}`;
};
const score = (metric: string, value: number) => metric === "accuracy"
  ? `${(value * 100).toFixed(2)}% accuracy`
  : `${value.toFixed(3)} RMSE`;
const holdoutFor = (id: string) => sampling.datasets.find((dataset) => dataset.id === id)!
  .methods.find((method) => method.id === "holdout")!;
const breastHoldout = holdoutFor("breast_cancer");
const diabetesHoldout = holdoutFor("diabetes");
const stopCounts = (
  method: { converged: number; capped: number },
  seeds: number,
) => {
  const other = seeds - method.converged - method.capped;
  return [
    `${method.converged}/${seeds} converged`,
    method.capped > 0 ? `${method.capped} capped` : null,
    other > 0 ? `${other} other stops` : null,
  ].filter(Boolean).join(" · ");
};
---

<section id="sampling" aria-labelledby="sampling-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Hyperparameter search</p>
    <h2 id="sampling-title">Fixed holdout and short cross-validation</h2>
    <p class="lead">
      A fixed holdout replaces five inner training and hypergradient solves per evaluation with one.
      This study compares that shortcut with a short five-fold search and with tuning on fewer
      training rows before a short five-fold search.
    </p>
    <p>
      On Breast Cancer Wisconsin, holdout gave a median paired speedup of {speed(breastHoldout.speedup)}
      with a median test accuracy difference of {delta("accuracy", breastHoldout.delta)} percentage points.
      On Diabetes, the corresponding values were {speed(diabetesHoldout.speedup)} and
      {" "}{delta("rmse", diabetesHoldout.delta)} test RMSE. Full CV and holdout converged on every split.
      Most short searches reached their iteration budget.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each dataset uses five paired 80/20 development/test splits and one thread.
      The fixed holdout reuses the first of the five development folds throughout the search.
      The outer test set is reserved for scoring the final model.
      Features of the real datasets are standardized on the full development set before the inner
      split. All protocols use that same transformation.
    </p>

    <div class="sampling-grid">
      {sampling.datasets.map((dataset) => (
        <div class="sampling-dataset">
          <h3 id={`sampling-${dataset.id}`}>{dataset.label}</h3>
          <p class="dataset-meta">
            {dataset.kind === "real" ? "Real data" : "Synthetic data"} · {dataset.samples} observations ·{" "}
            {dataset.metric === "accuracy" ? "classification" : "regression"}
            {dataset.source && <> · <a href={dataset.source}>Dataset source</a></>}
          </p>
          <div class="card table-scroll" role="region" aria-labelledby={`sampling-${dataset.id}`} tabindex="0">
            <table>
              <caption>Median paired differences and ranges relative to full CV</caption>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">Search protocol</th>
                  <th scope="col">Speedup</th>
                  <th scope="col">{dataset.metric === "accuracy" ? "Accuracy Δ (pp)" : "RMSE Δ"}</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                {dataset.methods.map((method) => (
                  <tr>
                    <th scope="row">
                      {method.label}
                      <span class="detail">{stopCounts(method, dataset.seeds)}</span>
                    </th>
                    <td>
                      {speed(method.speedup)}
                      <span class="detail">{method.id === "cv5" ? seconds(method.seconds)
                        : `${speed(method.speedup_min)} to ${speed(method.speedup_max)}`}</span>
                    </td>
                    <td>
                      {delta(dataset.metric, method.delta)}
                      <span class="detail">{method.id === "cv5" ? score(dataset.metric, method.score)
                        : `${delta(dataset.metric, method.delta_min)} to ${delta(dataset.metric, method.delta_max)}`}</span>
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <p class="sampling-note">
      Reference times and test scores in the full CV rows are medians. Other rows show the median
      and range of per-split speedups and test score differences against the reference on the same
      split. Positive accuracy differences are better and negative RMSE differences are better.
      RMSE is in the original target units. A capped run exhausted its iteration budget in the
      final tuning stage.
    </p>
    <p class="sampling-note">
      Full CV and fixed holdout allow up to forty L-BFGS-B iterations. Short CV allows five.
      The subset protocols sample half of the first fold's training rows once, keep its validation
      rows and tune for up to ten iterations. They pass the selected hyperparameters to a fresh
      search capped at five iterations on all five folds. The scaled protocol adjusts λ by the
      training-size ratio and reverses that adjustment before full CV. The direct protocol
      transfers λ unchanged. Timings include every refit, including the extra refit at the end of
      subset tuning.
    </p>
    <p class="sampling-note">
      <a href={`${raw}/hpo_sampling_web.csv`}>Per-split results (CSV)</a> ·
      <a href={`${raw}/hpo_sampling_web.txt`}>Run log and reproduction command</a> ·
      <a href={`${raw}/hpo_holdout.py`}>Benchmark script</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .sampling-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 31rem), 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .sampling-dataset {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .sampling-dataset h3 {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .dataset-meta,
  .sampling-note {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  .dataset-meta {
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .sampling-dataset table {
    width: 100%;
  }
  caption {
    text-align: left;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }
  th[scope="row"] {
    font-weight: 600;
    white-space: normal;
    min-width: 8.2rem;
  }
  td {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  th,
  td {
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .detail {
    display: block;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
</style>
